---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/docs.astro";
---

<DocsLayout title="Trigger API and Run now — Querial">
    <div class="space-y-8">
        <div>
            <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-querial-sky">For DevOps</p>
            <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold mt-1">Trigger API and Run now</h1>
        </div>
        <div class="prose dark:prose-invert max-w-none space-y-6 [&>p]:text-muted-foreground [&>h2]:text-foreground [&>h3]:text-foreground">
            <p>
                External systems start a published deployment with
                <code class="text-foreground">POST /api/trigger</code> on the API host,
                using a Bearer API key. Web <strong class="text-foreground">Run now</strong>
                uses the same contract (session cookie). Schedules create runs without a
                body; they cannot attach Parquet files. Developers design the graph;
                this role mints keys, binds deployments, and calls the API.
            </p>

            <h2>API keys</h2>
            <p>
                Keys live under Workers in Workspace. Prefix
                <code class="text-foreground">qk_</code>, SHA-256 at rest, shown in full
                once. Scopes: <code class="text-foreground">trigger_run</code>,
                <code class="text-foreground">view_status</code>,
                <code class="text-foreground">cancel_run</code>, with optional environment
                restriction. A key cannot act as Platform admin and cannot reach another
                project.
            </p>
            <div class="overflow-x-auto not-prose">
                <table class="w-full text-sm">
                    <thead><tr class="border-b border-border text-left"><th class="py-2 pr-4">Kind</th><th class="py-2 pr-4">Bound deployment</th><th class="py-2">May call</th></tr></thead>
                    <tbody class="text-muted-foreground">
                        <tr class="border-b border-border/50"><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-foreground">Project-scoped</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">None</td><td class="py-2">Any deployment in that project (then env scopes). <code class="text-foreground">deploymentId</code> required on trigger.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-foreground">Deployment-scoped</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">One deployment</td><td class="py-2">Only that deployment. Mismatch is 404. <code class="text-foreground">deploymentId</code> may be omitted or must match.</td></tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>
            <p>
                Primary UX: generate from Deployment details. Api Keys admin can create
                either kind. Project setting
                <code class="text-foreground">allow_project_scoped_api_keys</code>
                (default on): when off, existing project-scoped keys stay listed, but
                trigger / contract / status / cancel return <strong class="text-foreground">403</strong>.
                New project-scoped create is 400. Rotate of an existing project-scoped
                row is allowed; the new secret still 403s until the setting is on.
                Deployment-scoped keys are unaffected. Toggle is project Admin.
            </p>
            <p>
                Cross-project or a bound key aimed at the wrong deployment is
                <strong class="text-foreground">404</strong>, not 403 — do not use status
                codes to probe other projects.
            </p>

            <h2>Trigger contract</h2>
            <p>
                Before you POST, load the schema the version actually needs:
            </p>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
                <li><code class="text-foreground">GET /api/deployments/{"{id}"}/trigger-contract</code> — Bearer or session</li>
                <li><code class="text-foreground">GET /api/trigger-contract</code> — deployment-scoped keys only</li>
            </ul>
            <p>
                The payload lists parameter codes with <code class="text-foreground">paramType</code>
                and effective values, plus parquet input slots (<code class="text-foreground">outputName</code>,
                resolved <code class="text-foreground">retentionDays</code>). Secrets on
                the contract are redacted or omitted. Web Run now renders the same form.
            </p>

            <h2>JSON trigger (parameters only)</h2>
            <pre class="rounded-xl border border-border/50 bg-muted/40 p-4 text-sm overflow-x-auto"><code>{`POST /api/trigger
Authorization: Bearer qk_…
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "deploymentId": "…",
  "idempotencyKey": "customer-a-2026-07-30",
  "parameters": {
    "windowStart": "2026-07-30T00:00:00Z"
  }
}`}</code></pre>
            <p>
                If the published version has any
                <code class="text-foreground">external-parquet</code> step, JSON is
                <strong class="text-foreground">400</strong> — use multipart. Unknown
                parameter codes, empty required values, and type mismatches are 400.
                Pool / agent / <code class="text-foreground">assignment</code> JSON is
                not accepted.
            </p>

            <h2>Multipart trigger (parameters and files)</h2>
            <p>
                One request. Parts:
            </p>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
                <li><code class="text-foreground">deploymentId</code> — required for project-scoped keys</li>
                <li><code class="text-foreground">idempotencyKey</code> — optional</li>
                <li><code class="text-foreground">parameters</code> — UTF-8 JSON object (same map as JSON trigger)</li>
                <li>One file named <code class="text-foreground">parquet.{"{outputName}"}</code> per ingest slot</li>
            </ul>
            <p>
                Extra parts, missing required files, garbage bytes, or oversize uploads
                are 400 with <em>no</em> run created. Success is
                <strong class="text-foreground">200</strong>
                <code class="text-foreground">{"{ runId, isIdempotentReplay }"}</code>.
            </p>

            <h2>Parameter merge</h2>
            <pre class="rounded-xl border border-border/50 bg-muted/40 p-4 text-sm overflow-x-auto"><code>effective[code] = trigger overlay ?? deployment override ?? pipeline default</code></pre>
            <p>
                Types: <code class="text-foreground">string</code>,
                <code class="text-foreground">integer</code>,
                <code class="text-foreground">decimal</code>,
                <code class="text-foreground">boolean</code>,
                <code class="text-foreground">datetime</code>,
                <code class="text-foreground">date</code>. Plan JSON stays redacted;
                the overlay is stored for execution bind. Uploading Parquet does not
                skip this validation.
            </p>

            <h2>Idempotency</h2>
            <p>
                Unique per <code class="text-foreground">(project, deployment, key)</code>
                for 24 hours. Fingerprint is the canonical merged parameter map (secret-like
                values hashed) plus sorted <code class="text-foreground">outputName → SHA-256</code>
                of each file. Same key and same fingerprint replays
                (<code class="text-foreground">isIdempotentReplay: true</code>). Same key,
                different params or bytes → <strong class="text-foreground">409</strong>.
            </p>

            <h2>Web Run now</h2>
            <p>
                If the contract has any parameters or any parquet inputs, the modal
                opens. One-click remains only when both arrays are empty. Empty secret
                fields mean “keep the deployment value.” Developers cannot trigger
                Production via a key any more than they can in the UI.
            </p>

            <h2>Status and cancel</h2>
            <p>
                Same Bearer key. Use the scopes minted on the key. Disabled project-scoped
                keys 403 on these routes too. Feature flag for API keys off → 503 on the
                anonymous Bearer route.
            </p>
            <p>
                Ingest versions cannot be scheduled —
                <a href="/docs/developer-external-parquet" class="text-link hover:underline">External Parquet ingest</a>.
                Keys overview also lives on
                <a href="/docs/devops-agents" class="text-link hover:underline">Agents, API keys, and Git</a>.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>
</DocsLayout>
